John,

I have noticed that the reference grammar's description of the 
interactions between the "lexical" cmavo differs from that in the YACC 
grammar. In particular, they differ in describing the precedence of ZOI 
and LOhU as compared with ZO and SI/SA/SU. For example, if you believe 
the description in the YACC, "zoi si" clearly begins a non-Lojban quote, 
to be terminated by ".si". However, if you believe the refgrammar, the 
"si" erases the "zoi".

Which is right?

Clark Nelson

